  ($q$pd-604$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Probability$q$, 2, null, $q$A box holds 6 red pens and 8 blue pens. Two pens are chosen at random without replacement. What is the probability that both are red?$q$, $q$["9/49","4/9","15/91","3/7"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$P(first red) = 6/14; P(second red) = 5/13. The product is 15/91.$q$),
