  ($q$pd-606$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$q$, $q$Evaluating statistical claims$q$, 2, null, $q$A town's records show that months with higher the number of firefighters sent also tend to have higher the amount of damage at a fire. Which statement is best supported by this observational data alone?$q$, $q$["Higher the amount of damage at a fire cause higher the number of firefighters sent.","The number of firefighters sent and the amount of damage at a fire are unrelated.","Higher the number of firefighters sent cause higher the amount of damage at a fire.","The number of firefighters sent and the amount of damage at a fire are associated, but the data alone do not show that one causes the other."]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Observational data can reveal association; a third factor may explain both, so causation is not established.$q$),
