  ($q$geo-519$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Coordinate geometry$q$, 1, null, $q$In the xy-plane, what is the distance between the points (−1, 3) and (19, 24)?$q$, $q$["41","30","1","29"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Distance = √(20² + 21²) = √841 = 29.$q$),
  ($q$geo-520$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Special right triangles$q$, 2, null, $q$The hypotenuse of a right triangle with two congruent sides is 3√2. What is the area of the triangle?$q$, $q$["4.5","18","3","9"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The legs of a 45°-45°-90° triangle are hypotenuse/√2 = 3. Area = ½ × 3 × 3 = 4.5.$q$),
  ($q$geo-521$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Circles$q$, 2, null, $q$A circle has a radius of 8. What is the length of an arc of the circle with a central angle of 60°?$q$, $q$["4π/3","8π/3","32π/3","96π"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Arc length = (60/360) × 2π(8) = 8π/3.$q$),
  ($q$geo-522$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Right triangle trigonometry$q$, 2, null, $q$In right triangle ABC, the right angle is at C, AB = 25, BC = 7, and AC = 24. What is the value of tan A?$q$, $q$["7/25","24/7","7/24","24/25"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$For angle A, the opposite side is 7, the adjacent side is 24, and the hypotenuse is 25. tan = opposite/adjacent = 7/24.$q$),
  ($q$geo-523$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Right triangle trigonometry$q$, 2, null, $q$In right triangle ABC, the right angle is at C, AB = 5, BC = 3, and AC = 4. What is the value of sin A?$q$, $q$["3/4","4/3","4/5","3/5"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$For angle A, the opposite side is 3, the adjacent side is 4, and the hypotenuse is 5. sin = opposite/hypotenuse = 3/5.$q$),
  ($q$geo-524$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Circles$q$, 2, null, $q$The equation x² + y² − 4x − 2y = 4 defines a circle in the xy-plane. What is the radius of the circle?$q$, $q$["4","3","5","9"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Complete the square: (x − 2)² + (y − 1)² = 4 + 4 + 1 = 9. So the radius is √9 = 3.$q$),
