  ($q$geo-526$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Lines and angles$q$, 1, null, $q$Two angles form a straight line. One angle measures x° and the other measures 4x°. What is the value of x?$q$, $q$["30","36","45","144"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Angles on a straight line sum to 180°: x + 4x = 180, so 5x = 180 and x = 36.$q$),
  ($q$geo-527$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Area and volume$q$, 1, null, $q$A rectangle has a perimeter of 42 and a width of 5. What is the area of the rectangle?$q$, $q$["256","210","185","80"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Perimeter = 2(w + l), so 42 = 2(5 + l) and l = 16. Area = 5 × 16 = 80.$q$),
  ($q$geo-528$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Area and volume$q$, 2, null, $q$A right circular cylinder has a volume of 36π and a radius of 3. What is the height of the cylinder?$q$, $q$["7","36","12","4"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Volume = πr²h gives 36π = π(3)²h, so h = 36/9 = 4.$q$),
  ($q$geo-529$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Circles$q$, 2, null, $q$The equation x² + y² − 8x − 2y = 8 defines a circle in the xy-plane. What is the radius of the circle?$q$, $q$["7","25","8","5"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Complete the square: (x − 4)² + (y − 1)² = 8 + 16 + 1 = 25. So the radius is √25 = 5.$q$),
