  ($q$geo-531$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Area and volume$q$, 1, null, $q$A rectangular box has a length of 4, a width of 8, and a height of 5. What is the volume of the box?$q$, $q$["37","184","17","160"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Volume = length × width × height = 4 × 8 × 5 = 160.$q$),
  ($q$geo-532$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Circles$q$, 1, null, $q$A circle has a circumference of 14π. What is the area of the circle?$q$, $q$["49π","14π","7π","196π"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Circumference = 2πr = 14π, so r = 7. Area = πr² = 49π.$q$),
  ($q$geo-533$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Lines and angles$q$, 2, null, $q$Two angles form a linear pair. One angle measures x° and the other measures (3x + 16)°. What is the value of x?$q$, $q$["45","161","51","41"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The angles of a linear pair are supplementary: x + (3x + 16) = 180. So 4x = 164 and x = 41.$q$),
  ($q$geo-534$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Right triangles$q$, 1, null, $q$In a right triangle, the two legs have lengths 20 and 21. What is the length of the hypotenuse?$q$, $q$["1","30","29","41"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$By the Pythagorean theorem, 20² + 21² = 841 = 29², so the hypotenuse is 29.$q$),
  ($q$geo-535$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Similar triangles$q$, 2, null, $q$Triangle ABC is similar to triangle DEF, where AB corresponds to DE and BC corresponds to EF. AB = 2, BC = 5, and DE = 8. What is the length of EF?$q$, $q$["9","11","20","22"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The scale factor from ABC to DEF is 8/2 = 4. So EF = 4 × 5 = 20.$q$),
  ($q$geo-536$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Triangle angles$q$, 2, null, $q$In isosceles triangle PQR, PQ = PR and the measure of angle P is 140°. What is the measure of angle Q, in degrees?$q$, $q$["20","70","160","40"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The base angles Q and R are equal and sum to 180 − 140 = 40, so each is 20°.$q$),
  ($q$geo-537$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Circles$q$, 2, null, $q$The equation (x + 4)² + y² = 16 defines a circle in the xy-plane. What is the radius of the circle?$q$, $q$["8","2","4","16"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$In (x − h)² + (y − k)² = r², the right side is r². Here r² = 16, so r = 4.$q$),
  ($q$geo-538$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Coordinate geometry$q$, 2, null, $q$A triangle has vertices at (0, 0), (11, 0), and (0, 3). What is the area of the triangle?$q$, $q$["16.5","14","27.5","8.25"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The legs along the axes have lengths 11 and 3, so the area is (1/2)(11)(3) = 16.5.$q$),
  ($q$geo-539$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Similar triangles$q$, 2, null, $q$A 4-foot post casts a shadow 3 feet long. At the same time, a nearby tree casts a shadow 18 feet long. How tall is the tree, in feet?$q$, $q$["22","18","21","24"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The triangles are similar: tree/18 = 4/3, so the tree is 4 × 6 = 24 feet tall.$q$),
  ($q$geo-540$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Special right triangles$q$, 1, null, $q$In a 45°-45°-90° triangle, each leg has length 3. What is the length of the hypotenuse?$q$, $q$["6","3√3","9","3√2"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The hypotenuse of a 45°-45°-90° triangle is the leg times √2: 3√2.$q$),
  ($q$geo-541$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Lines and angles$q$, 2, null, $q$Two parallel lines are cut by a transversal. Two same-side interior angles measure (4x + 19)° and (x + 31)°. What is the value of x?$q$, $q$["26","21","31","46"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Same-side interior angles are supplementary: 4x + 19 + x + 31 = 180 → 5x = 130 → x = 26.$q$),
  ($q$geo-542$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Circles$q$, 1, null, $q$A circle in the xy-plane has equation (x + 1)² + (y − 6)² = 64. What is the radius of the circle?$q$, $q$["9","8","64","4"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$In (x − h)² + (y − k)² = r², the right side is r². Here r² = 64, so r = 8.$q$),
  ($q$geo-543$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Right triangle trigonometry$q$, 2, null, $q$In a right triangle, one acute angle measures 10°. If sin 10° = p, which of the following is equal to cos 80°?$q$, $q$["1 − p","1/p","√(1 − p²)","p"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Sine and cosine of complementary angles are equal: cos(90° − x°) = sin x°. So cos 80° = sin 10° = p.$q$),
  ($q$geo-544$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Special right triangles$q$, 1, null, $q$In a 30°-60°-90° triangle, the shorter leg has length 10. What is the length of the hypotenuse?$q$, $q$["10√2","20","12","10√3"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$In a 30°-60°-90° triangle the hypotenuse is twice the shorter leg: 20.$q$),
