  ($q$geo-605$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Area and volume$q$, 1, null, $q$A right circular cylinder has radius 9 and height 3. What is the volume of the cylinder?$q$, $q$["486π","84π","243π","54π"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$V = πr²h = π(9)²(3) = 243π.$q$),
  ($q$geo-606$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Similar triangles$q$, 2, null, $q$A 6-foot post casts a shadow 4 feet long. At the same time, a nearby tree casts a shadow 20 feet long. How tall is the tree, in feet?$q$, $q$["26","30","34","20"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The triangles are similar: tree/20 = 6/4, so the tree is 6 × 5 = 30 feet tall.$q$),
  ($q$geo-607$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Circles$q$, 1, null, $q$A circle has an area of 49π square units. What is the circumference of the circle?$q$, $q$["98π","49π","7π","14π"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$πr² = 49π gives r = 7, so the circumference is 2πr = 14π.$q$),
  ($q$geo-608$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Right triangles$q$, 2, null, $q$A right triangle has legs of length x and x + 7, and its hypotenuse has length 13. What is the perimeter of the triangle?$q$, $q$["44","33","17","30"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$x² + (x + 7)² = 169 → 2x² + 14x − 120 = 0 → x = 5. The legs are 5 and 12, so the perimeter is 5 + 12 + 13 = 30.$q$),
  ($q$geo-609$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Coordinate geometry$q$, 2, null, $q$A triangle has vertices at (0, 0), (4, 0), and (0, 12). What is the area of the triangle?$q$, $q$["24","16","28","12"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The legs along the axes have lengths 4 and 12, so the area is (1/2)(4)(12) = 24.$q$),
  ($q$geo-610$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Right triangles$q$, 2, null, $q$A rectangle has a length of 24 and a diagonal of 26. What is the area of the rectangle?$q$, $q$["240","34","68","624"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The width is √(26² − 24²) = 10. Area = 24 × 10 = 240.$q$),
  ($q$geo-611$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Circles$q$, 1, null, $q$A circle in the xy-plane has equation (x + 3)² + (y + 1)² = 81. What is the radius of the circle?$q$, $q$["10","81","9","18"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$In (x − h)² + (y − k)² = r², the right side is r². Here r² = 81, so r = 9.$q$),
  ($q$geo-612$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Right triangle trigonometry$q$, 2, null, $q$In right triangle PQR, the right angle is at Q and tan P = 3/4. If PQ = 8, what is the length of QR?$q$, $q$["8","10","3","6"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$tan P = QR/PQ, so QR = 8 × 3/4 = 6.$q$),
  ($q$geo-613$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Right triangles$q$, 2, null, $q$A ladder 10 feet long leans against a vertical wall. The base of the ladder is 6 feet from the wall. How high up the wall, in feet, does the ladder reach?$q$, $q$["4","8","16","9"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The ladder, wall, and ground form a right triangle: height = √(10² − 6²) = 8 feet.$q$),
  ($q$geo-614$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Similar triangles$q$, 2, null, $q$Triangle ABC is similar to triangle DEF with a ratio of corresponding sides AB:DE = 1:3. The perimeter of triangle ABC is 12. What is the perimeter of triangle DEF?$q$, $q$["108","36","48","4"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Perimeters scale by the same ratio as the sides: 12 × 3 = 36.$q$),
