  ($q$geo-616$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Area and volume$q$, 2, null, $q$The total surface area of a cube is 486 square units. What is the volume of the cube, in cubic units?$q$, $q$["54","4374","81","729"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Each of the 6 faces has area 81, so the edge length is 9. Volume = 9³ = 729.$q$),
  ($q$geo-618$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Triangle angles$q$, 2, null, $q$In triangle PQR, angles P and Q measure 77° and 41°. The exterior angle at R, formed by extending side PR, is adjacent to the interior angle at R. What is its measure, in degrees?$q$, $q$["103","242","62","118"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$An exterior angle equals the sum of the two remote interior angles: 77° + 41° = 118°.$q$),
  ($q$geo-619$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Special right triangles$q$, 2, null, $q$In a 30°-60°-90° triangle, the shorter leg has length 6. What is the length of the longer leg?$q$, $q$["6√3","18","12","6√2"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The longer leg is the shorter leg times √3: 6√3.$q$),
  ($q$geo-620$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Coordinate geometry$q$, 2, null, $q$A triangle has vertices at (0, 0), (8, 0), and (0, 8). What is the area of the triangle?$q$, $q$["40","16","32","64"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The legs along the axes have lengths 8 and 8, so the area is (1/2)(8)(8) = 32.$q$),
  ($q$geo-621$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Lines and angles$q$, 2, null, $q$Lines ℓ and m are parallel and are cut by a transversal. One angle measures (3x − 5)° and its alternate interior angle measures (x + 4)°. What is the value of x?$q$, $q$["45","171","6","9"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Alternate interior angles are equal: 3x − 5 = x + 4 → 2x = 9 → x = 9.$q$),
  ($q$geo-622$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Area and volume$q$, 2, null, $q$A right circular cylinder has a radius of 5 and a volume of 250π. What is the height of the cylinder?$q$, $q$["25","250","20","10"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$πr²h = 250π → 25h = 250 → h = 10.$q$),
  ($q$geo-623$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Right triangle trigonometry$q$, 1, null, $q$In right triangle PQR, the right angle is at R, PR = 10, QR = 24, and PQ = 26. What is tan P?$q$, $q$["13/12","13/5","1","12/5"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Relative to angle P, the opposite side is 24, the adjacent side is 10, and the hypotenuse is 26. tan P = 12/5.$q$),
  ($q$geo-624$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Special right triangles$q$, 2, null, $q$The hypotenuse of a 45°-45°-90° triangle is 4√2. What is the area of the triangle?$q$, $q$["4","32","8","16"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Each leg equals the hypotenuse divided by √2, so each leg is 4. The area is (1/2)(4)(4) = 8.$q$),
  ($q$geo-625$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Triangle angles$q$, 2, null, $q$In isosceles triangle ABC, AB = AC and the measure of angle A is 64°. What is the measure of angle B, in degrees?$q$, $q$["116","58","68","26"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The base angles are equal and the angles sum to 180°, so angle B = (180° − 64°)/2 = 58°.$q$),
  ($q$geo-626$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Coordinate geometry$q$, 1, null, $q$What are the coordinates of the midpoint of the line segment with endpoints (8, −4) and (18, −2)?$q$, $q$["(5, 1)","(−3, 13)","(13, −3)","(26, −6)"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Midpoint = ((8 + 18)/2, (−4 − 2)/2) = (13, −3).$q$),
  ($q$geo-627$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Geometry and Trigonometry$q$, $q$Area and volume$q$, 2, null, $q$A right circular cylinder has a radius of 6 and a volume of 108π. What is the height of the cylinder?$q$, $q$["6","108","18","3"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$πr²h = 108π → 36h = 108 → h = 3.$q$),
